; `<>` in an executable position IS the program, so it runs: genuine self-
; application, with no base case of its own. The gate is what bounds it — the
; program re-enters itself only while the host keeps answering 0.
;
; Two calls minimum: the question, then the branch. A host that answers 1 first
; stops immediately, which is why this asserts a floor rather than a count.
; expect: calls >=2
; expect: clean
; expect: answers
(% "Answer with exactly the single character: 1"
   "Answer with exactly the word: done"
   <>)
